  "result": "Perfect! All 159 tests pass. Added payment terms support to invoices.\n\n**Changes to src/invoices.js:**\n\n1. **New helper function `calculateDueDate(issueDate, terms)`**:\n   - NET14: issue date + 14 days\n   - NET30: issue date + 30 days\n   - EOM: last day of the issue date's month (handles leap years correctly)\n\n2. **Updated `createInvoice()` signature**:\n   - Accepts optional `terms` parameter (defaults to 'NET30')\n   - Validates terms against valid options\n   - Returns TERMS_INVALID for unknown terms\n   - Sets `invoice.terms` and `invoice.dueDate` in returned object\n\n**Added to src/errors.js:**\n- `TERMS_INVALID`: Error for invalid payment term values\n\n**Tests added (7 new tests):**\n- \u2713 Default NET30 terms applied\n- \u2713 NET14, NET30, EOM all work correctly\n- \u2713 EOM handles different months (including Feb 29 in leap years)\n- \u2713 Invalid terms rejected with TERMS_INVALID\n- \u2713 Terms preserved through invoice modifications\n\n**Key behavior:**\n- Default to NET30 if terms not specified\n- Due dates calculated correctly across month/year boundaries\n- Terms and dueDate preserved when invoice is modified\n- EOM correctly identifies last day of month (handles leap years)\n\nAll 159 tests pass.",
